1
00:00:33,346 --> 00:00:38,059
‎AGENT KIM REACTIVATED

2
00:00:40,937 --> 00:00:43,106
‎NORTH HAMGYONG PROVINCE, NORTH KOREA

3
00:00:51,823 --> 00:00:53,741
‎EPISODE 4

4
00:00:53,825 --> 00:00:56,286
‎GEUMGANG ORPHANAGE

5
00:00:57,495 --> 00:00:58,913
‎Nice to meet you.

6
00:00:58,997 --> 00:01:01,916
‎I'm Major Ri Eung Ryeong

7
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:03,668
‎of the Democratic People's Republic
‎of Korea.

8
00:01:03,751 --> 00:01:07,005
‎I hear that you're the most agile

9
00:01:07,088 --> 00:01:09,674
‎and physically fit students here.

10
00:01:09,757 --> 00:01:12,677
‎If you think you're the best of them all

11
00:01:13,261 --> 00:01:16,306
‎and want to become a member
‎of the Republic's athletic corps,

12
00:01:16,389 --> 00:01:17,557
‎step forward.

13
00:01:19,475 --> 00:01:21,227
‎If I become a member,

14
00:01:21,311 --> 00:01:22,687
‎will I be able to eat my fill?

15
00:01:23,855 --> 00:01:24,856
‎You will.

16
00:01:28,735 --> 00:01:30,945
‎YOUNG REVOLUTIONARIES
‎OF THE LEARNING-FIRST DOCTRINE

17
00:01:38,536 --> 00:01:39,871
‎Move the desks.

18
00:01:45,960 --> 00:01:47,045
‎You're the only one who passed.

19
00:01:48,421 --> 00:01:49,464
‎Tell me your name.

20
00:01:52,884 --> 00:01:53,968
‎Park Yeong Gwang, sir.

21
00:01:54,552 --> 00:01:55,511
‎Take him to the car.

22
00:01:56,763 --> 00:01:58,139
‎Yes, sir.

23
00:02:08,191 --> 00:02:09,442
‎That one passes too.

24
00:02:10,276 --> 00:02:11,486
‎A warrior of the Republic

25
00:02:12,070 --> 00:02:14,572
‎ought to have that kind of tenacity.

26
00:02:17,742 --> 00:02:18,576
‎Hey.

27
00:02:19,577 --> 00:02:20,912
‎What's your name?

28
00:02:21,746 --> 00:02:22,747
‎Kim…

29
00:02:36,177 --> 00:02:38,263
‎ARMED WITH REVOLUTIONARY SPIRIT

30
00:02:45,853 --> 00:02:48,064
‎Stand straight! Attention!

31
00:02:48,648 --> 00:02:51,943
‎All of you have become official members
‎of the Special Operations Unit

32
00:02:52,026 --> 00:02:55,363
‎of the Democratic People's Republic
‎of Korea.

33
00:02:55,446 --> 00:02:56,781
‎Our goal

34
00:02:56,864 --> 00:02:58,783
‎is to infiltrate the South

35
00:02:58,866 --> 00:03:01,619
‎and bring back the heads
‎of their leading officials!

36
00:03:03,413 --> 00:03:05,373
‎Take them to the torture chamber.

37
00:03:05,456 --> 00:03:09,293
‎-We are the people's army
‎-We are the people's army

38
00:03:09,377 --> 00:03:12,797
‎-and warriors of belief and conviction.
‎-and warriors of belief and conviction.

39
00:03:12,880 --> 00:03:13,715
‎Stop!

40
00:03:16,634 --> 00:03:18,928
‎You still think
‎this is the athletic corps?

41
00:03:19,595 --> 00:03:20,680
‎This is hell.

42
00:03:20,763 --> 00:03:22,640
‎You'll either survive
‎and become an operative,

43
00:03:22,724 --> 00:03:24,225
‎or you'll die and become pig feed!

44
00:03:24,934 --> 00:03:26,352
‎It's one or the other.

45
00:03:27,311 --> 00:03:28,146
‎Number 66.

46
00:03:29,105 --> 00:03:30,857
‎What's your name?

47
00:03:32,525 --> 00:03:34,527
‎I don't remember, sir.

48
00:03:36,529 --> 00:03:37,405
‎Number 73.

49
00:03:38,614 --> 00:03:40,283
‎What's your name?

50
00:03:42,160 --> 00:03:42,994
‎Kim…

51
00:03:43,619 --> 00:03:46,289
‎I only know that my last name is Kim.

52
00:03:47,373 --> 00:03:49,709
‎This bastard still doesn't get it.

53
00:03:51,419 --> 00:03:54,047
‎Wild animals don't have names!

54
00:03:55,465 --> 00:03:58,801
‎None of you have first or last names.

55
00:03:58,885 --> 00:04:00,053
‎Do you understand?

56
00:04:00,136 --> 00:04:01,304
‎Do you?!

57
00:04:06,267 --> 00:04:10,730
‎-Defend with our lives!
‎-Defend with our lives!

58
00:04:10,813 --> 00:04:13,524
‎-Defend with our lives!
‎-Defend with our lives!

59
00:04:13,608 --> 00:04:15,860
‎-Defend with our lives!
‎-Defend with our lives!

60
00:04:15,943 --> 00:04:17,737
‎-Hurry up! Get over here!
‎-Defend with our lives!

61
00:04:17,820 --> 00:04:18,654
‎Right now!

62
00:04:18,738 --> 00:04:19,989
‎Hurry up!

63
00:04:20,907 --> 00:04:21,866
‎Get it together!

64
00:04:24,118 --> 00:04:25,995
‎-Hurry up!
‎-Speed it up.

65
00:04:29,582 --> 00:04:30,541
‎Hurry up!

66
00:04:30,625 --> 00:04:31,459
‎Fire!

67
00:04:49,477 --> 00:04:51,521
‎CRUSH THE PROVOCATIVE SCHEMES
‎OF THE SOUTH KOREAN PUPPETS!

68
00:05:03,866 --> 00:05:04,742
‎Enough.

69
00:05:06,119 --> 00:05:07,161
‎Number 66.

70
00:05:07,870 --> 00:05:10,456
‎You are truly
‎the Republic's finest warrior.

71
00:05:10,957 --> 00:05:12,166
‎Well done.

72
00:05:32,437 --> 00:05:33,521
‎Forget it.

73
00:05:34,188 --> 00:05:35,022
‎Take it away.

74
00:05:35,523 --> 00:05:37,525
‎I'm not giving it to you out of pity.

75
00:05:37,608 --> 00:05:39,735
‎You keep losing to me,

76
00:05:39,819 --> 00:05:42,196
‎so I was wondering
‎if it's because you don't eat enough.

77
00:05:43,114 --> 00:05:44,115
‎Get lost.

78
00:05:44,198 --> 00:05:46,951
‎Come on. We're from the same orphanage.

79
00:05:51,164 --> 00:05:53,541
‎Don't let pride get in the way
‎between comrades.

80
00:05:53,624 --> 00:05:55,209
‎You bastard!

81
00:05:55,293 --> 00:05:57,420
‎Go stuff your own face!

82
00:05:57,503 --> 00:05:59,630
‎Those two are at it again! Stop them!

83
00:05:59,714 --> 00:06:01,799
‎-Stop it!
‎-Stop!

84
00:06:01,883 --> 00:06:03,926
‎-Hey, stop!
‎-Let go of him!

85
00:06:04,010 --> 00:06:05,803
‎-Stop already!
‎-That bastard!

86
00:06:06,387 --> 00:06:08,139
‎COMBAT READINESS IS A REVOLUTIONARY DUTY

87
00:06:10,641 --> 00:06:11,475
‎Next.

88
00:06:57,188 --> 00:07:00,149
‎…NUMBER 85, NUMBER 18, NUMBER 44

89
00:07:56,330 --> 00:08:00,209
‎This operation is a joint operation,

90
00:08:00,293 --> 00:08:02,253
‎so it comes with a bigger reward.

91
00:08:02,878 --> 00:08:04,463
‎You will complete it successfully

92
00:08:05,256 --> 00:08:08,342
‎and return to our country as heroes.

93
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:12,638
‎-Democratic People's Republic of Korea!
‎-Democratic People's Republic of Korea!

94
00:09:00,561 --> 00:09:04,023
‎GANGWON PROVINCE, REPUBLIC OF KOREA

95
00:10:37,158 --> 00:10:37,992
‎Wait.

96
00:10:57,803 --> 00:11:00,514
‎Your brother was the best operative

97
00:11:00,598 --> 00:11:02,767
‎this unit has ever seen.

98
00:11:03,267 --> 00:11:05,269
‎But during a mission,

99
00:11:05,352 --> 00:11:07,855
‎some rat-bastard stabbed him in the back

100
00:11:08,481 --> 00:11:09,899
‎and got him killed.

101
00:11:34,423 --> 00:11:36,842
‎That rat-bastard traitor

102
00:11:36,926 --> 00:11:39,720
‎killed all of his comrades,

103
00:11:39,803 --> 00:11:42,765
‎stole the number 66 from your brother,

104
00:11:42,848 --> 00:11:45,643
‎and became a lapdog for the South!

105
00:11:49,730 --> 00:11:50,564
‎Yeong Gwang!

106
00:11:51,190 --> 00:11:52,107
‎Yeong Gwang!

107
00:11:52,191 --> 00:11:55,319
‎Yeong Gwang!

108
00:11:55,402 --> 00:11:57,112
‎Don't leave me behind!

109
00:11:57,196 --> 00:11:58,030
‎-Yeong Gwang!
‎-Wait for me!

110
00:11:58,113 --> 00:11:59,907
‎I promise to succeed
‎and come back for you!

111
00:11:59,990 --> 00:12:00,866
‎Stay alive!

112
00:12:00,950 --> 00:12:03,077
‎You have to survive, okay?

113
00:12:03,160 --> 00:12:05,287
‎-Wait for me, Gang Seong!
‎-Yeong Gwang!

114
00:12:07,998 --> 00:12:10,584
‎Yeong Gwang!

115
00:12:11,252 --> 00:12:12,628
‎Yeong Gwang!

116
00:12:29,728 --> 00:12:31,647
‎AGENT KIM REACTIVATED

117
00:12:38,904 --> 00:12:40,489
‎Here you are.

118
00:12:44,952 --> 00:12:46,203
‎Fake 66.

119
00:12:56,255 --> 00:12:58,007
‎Damn it.

120
00:13:32,249 --> 00:13:33,459
‎Don't move!

121
00:13:33,542 --> 00:13:34,418
‎Hands up.

122
00:13:34,918 --> 00:13:35,753
‎Hands up!

123
00:13:40,132 --> 00:13:41,175
‎Put the gun down.

124
00:13:43,719 --> 00:13:45,262
‎Times sure have changed.

125
00:13:47,806 --> 00:13:49,058
‎-Wait, slow down.
‎-Why?

126
00:13:50,726 --> 00:13:52,811
‎There's the clue.

127
00:13:52,895 --> 00:13:55,773
‎Slow, slow.

128
00:13:56,398 --> 00:13:57,566
‎I said put it down.

129
00:14:09,244 --> 00:14:10,204
‎Hands on your head.

130
00:14:10,788 --> 00:14:11,830
‎Get down on your knees.

131
00:14:13,999 --> 00:14:17,961
‎Who are these sharp people
‎I'd like to thank?

132
00:14:20,047 --> 00:14:21,674
‎The woman is my co-worker,

133
00:14:21,757 --> 00:14:23,008
‎and the man…

134
00:14:24,259 --> 00:14:25,511
‎is the owner of my local dry cleaner.

135
00:14:26,136 --> 00:14:26,971
‎What?

136
00:14:28,555 --> 00:14:31,809
‎You don't seem surprised,
‎so I guess you already knew.

137
00:14:34,311 --> 00:14:37,231
‎I expected someone would be watching me.

138
00:14:39,108 --> 00:14:40,234
‎I suggest you surrender…

139
00:14:42,319 --> 00:14:43,696
‎Number 66.

140
00:14:46,031 --> 00:14:47,616
‎Mr. Kim.

141
00:14:47,700 --> 00:14:50,035
‎You violated your contract
‎with the government.

142
00:14:50,119 --> 00:14:50,953
‎Please surrender.

143
00:14:53,580 --> 00:14:54,540
‎Min-ji…

144
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:57,418
‎has been kidnapped.

145
00:14:58,210 --> 00:14:59,962
‎Please wait until I find her.

146
00:15:00,045 --> 00:15:02,881
‎Once I do, I'll turn myself in.

147
00:15:06,885 --> 00:15:07,970
‎I give you my word.

148
00:15:12,975 --> 00:15:14,143
‎No, wait…

149
00:15:14,226 --> 00:15:15,769
‎Mr. Kim!

150
00:15:16,270 --> 00:15:17,229
‎Mr. Kim!

151
00:17:06,588 --> 00:17:07,840
‎Are you okay? How bad is it?

152
00:17:10,134 --> 00:17:11,218
‎Bulletproof vest…

153
00:17:11,927 --> 00:17:13,303
‎I thought you were dead!

154
00:17:13,387 --> 00:17:14,596
‎Hey, help me up.

155
00:17:16,014 --> 00:17:17,015
‎Hurry up and come out.

156
00:17:17,641 --> 00:17:18,934
‎I just got shot!

157
00:17:19,017 --> 00:17:20,936
‎Don't be such a crybaby!

158
00:17:21,019 --> 00:17:22,187
‎That was a close call.

159
00:17:36,201 --> 00:17:37,452
‎You sure know how to stay busy.

160
00:17:38,078 --> 00:17:39,496
‎When did you get shot?

161
00:17:39,580 --> 00:17:42,124
‎Han-soo, do you have a trauma kit?

162
00:17:43,542 --> 00:17:45,586
‎It should be under the back…

163
00:17:46,253 --> 00:17:47,254
‎Let's go to a hospital.

164
00:17:47,921 --> 00:17:49,590
‎It's fine, it's just a graze.

165
00:17:49,673 --> 00:17:50,632
‎Keep going.

166
00:17:51,133 --> 00:17:51,967
‎Just go.

167
00:17:52,634 --> 00:17:55,637
‎You just got hit in the side by a bullet.

168
00:17:56,471 --> 00:17:59,349
‎Getting grazed still counts
‎as getting shot, doesn't it?

169
00:18:03,520 --> 00:18:05,314
‎Are you sure you'll be okay?

170
00:18:05,397 --> 00:18:07,691
‎Right here! Let me off here.

171
00:18:07,774 --> 00:18:09,067
‎Yes, right here.

172
00:18:09,151 --> 00:18:10,611
‎This is good. Thank you!

173
00:18:11,111 --> 00:18:12,237
‎Hey!

174
00:18:12,321 --> 00:18:13,197
‎Hey!

175
00:18:14,573 --> 00:18:15,741
‎Has the bleeding even stopped?

176
00:18:16,366 --> 00:18:18,202
‎Stop!

177
00:18:24,416 --> 00:18:25,417
‎No!

178
00:18:28,837 --> 00:18:29,838
‎What's going on?

179
00:18:31,215 --> 00:18:32,132
‎That punk…

180
00:18:32,216 --> 00:18:33,550
‎Why you little…

181
00:18:33,634 --> 00:18:34,801
‎You almost killed me!

182
00:18:34,885 --> 00:18:36,136
‎What are you, a damn deer?

183
00:18:36,220 --> 00:18:38,805
‎-You bumped me! I felt it!
‎-Why pop out of nowhere like that?!

184
00:18:38,889 --> 00:18:40,599
‎Let me talk first! Hey!

185
00:18:40,682 --> 00:18:42,976
‎What's going on?
‎What happened to Min-ji? Where is she?

186
00:18:43,060 --> 00:18:43,894
‎Who are these bastards?

187
00:18:43,977 --> 00:18:45,145
‎Who are they?!

188
00:18:45,229 --> 00:18:47,064
‎Who the hell…

189
00:18:47,147 --> 00:18:48,774
‎Who are these damn bastards?!

190
00:18:48,857 --> 00:18:50,484
‎They're dead meat!

191
00:18:50,567 --> 00:18:51,526
‎Damn it!

192
00:18:51,610 --> 00:18:53,445
‎-Hey, is it okay if I break this?
‎-Careful with that!

193
00:18:53,528 --> 00:18:55,155
‎Goddamn it!

194
00:18:56,073 --> 00:18:58,533
‎I'm good. Let's focus now.

195
00:18:58,617 --> 00:18:59,910
‎Hey, are you okay?

196
00:18:59,993 --> 00:19:00,994
‎Are you…

197
00:19:01,078 --> 00:19:02,162
‎Hey!

198
00:19:02,246 --> 00:19:04,039
‎You already got attacked?!

199
00:19:04,122 --> 00:19:05,249
‎That's a gunshot wound, right?

200
00:19:05,332 --> 00:19:07,209
‎I told you to be careful!

201
00:19:07,292 --> 00:19:10,128
‎What were you two going to do without me?

202
00:19:11,880 --> 00:19:13,215
‎I'm here now, so don't worry.

203
00:19:13,799 --> 00:19:14,841
‎Don't worry.

204
00:19:15,342 --> 00:19:16,343
‎Just think of it

205
00:19:16,426 --> 00:19:19,012
‎as an extra hole in your body
‎and tough it out.

206
00:19:20,097 --> 00:19:22,432
‎So nostrils, ears, and bullet wounds
‎are all just holes, huh?

207
00:19:22,516 --> 00:19:24,393
‎They're all the same to you, aren't they?

208
00:19:25,644 --> 00:19:27,521
‎I'm just saying.

209
00:19:27,604 --> 00:19:29,940
‎Come on, we've been shot at before!

210
00:19:30,023 --> 00:19:30,899
‎Just keep driving.

211
00:19:31,733 --> 00:19:32,818
‎Are you okay?

212
00:19:33,568 --> 00:19:34,945
‎By the way, where are we going?

213
00:19:35,028 --> 00:19:37,030
‎Hwasin Station to find a homeless guy.

214
00:19:37,114 --> 00:19:39,157
‎The homeless guy who found Min-ji's phone.

215
00:19:39,241 --> 00:19:42,536
‎SEONMIN-EUP

216
00:19:42,619 --> 00:19:44,288
‎Codename 66's current location.

217
00:19:45,497 --> 00:19:47,541
‎8-3, Gongdan-gil, Seonmin-eup.

218
00:19:47,624 --> 00:19:48,917
‎Park Jin-cheol has joined them.

219
00:19:56,216 --> 00:19:57,843
‎-Step on it.
‎-Yes, sir.

220
00:20:04,850 --> 00:20:05,684
‎Hey.

221
00:20:06,935 --> 00:20:07,811
‎Let's hurry.

222
00:20:11,481 --> 00:20:12,316
‎Hey, you.

223
00:20:13,775 --> 00:20:15,360
‎Go buy me a bottle of soju.

224
00:20:15,444 --> 00:20:17,112
‎Damn it. Why aren't you going?

225
00:20:18,030 --> 00:20:19,781
‎Want me to teach you a lesson, you punk?

226
00:20:20,407 --> 00:20:21,825
‎-Dad!
‎-Come here!

227
00:20:22,409 --> 00:20:23,452
‎-You little punk.
‎-What's wrong?

228
00:20:23,535 --> 00:20:25,787
‎-This man was shouting at me.
‎-Yeah?

229
00:20:25,871 --> 00:20:27,247
‎What is it? What about him?

230
00:20:27,331 --> 00:20:28,415
‎He went off on me.

231
00:20:29,082 --> 00:20:30,584
‎Hey, mister. You sleeping?

232
00:20:31,293 --> 00:20:32,210
‎Hey, mister!

233
00:20:42,095 --> 00:20:42,929
‎Who are you?

234
00:20:45,223 --> 00:20:47,017
‎You remember this phone, right?

235
00:20:47,601 --> 00:20:49,061
‎I heard you traded it
‎for a bottle of soju.

236
00:20:49,978 --> 00:20:50,812
‎Did I?

237
00:20:51,396 --> 00:20:52,689
‎Why do you ask?

238
00:20:52,773 --> 00:20:54,566
‎-Where did you get it?
‎-He probably stole it.

239
00:20:54,649 --> 00:20:55,609
‎"Stole it"?

240
00:20:55,692 --> 00:20:56,777
‎Look.

241
00:20:56,860 --> 00:20:58,653
‎I'm not a thief!

242
00:20:59,279 --> 00:21:00,113
‎I found it!

243
00:21:00,697 --> 00:21:02,783
‎When and where did you find it?

244
00:21:02,866 --> 00:21:05,702
‎Why do I have to tell you that?

245
00:21:05,786 --> 00:21:08,372
‎Because it's still illegal
‎to sell something you found.

246
00:21:08,455 --> 00:21:09,498
‎Should I call the cops?

247
00:21:11,124 --> 00:21:11,958
‎Yeah, go ahead.

248
00:21:12,042 --> 00:21:15,796
‎Three men are threatening
‎an innocent citizen.

249
00:21:16,296 --> 00:21:17,214
‎I'll call them myself.

250
00:21:17,798 --> 00:21:19,341
‎Let's just beat him until he talks.

251
00:21:19,424 --> 00:21:21,134
‎That's not a bad idea,

252
00:21:21,218 --> 00:21:22,636
‎but too many people will see us.

253
00:21:22,719 --> 00:21:24,846
‎There's an alley over there.
‎Just wait here.

254
00:21:24,930 --> 00:21:26,223
‎I'll escort him and be right back.

255
00:21:26,306 --> 00:21:28,016
‎-Why don't you come with me?
‎-No, wait.

256
00:21:28,100 --> 00:21:29,351
‎-Come on.
‎-He threw it away.

257
00:21:30,519 --> 00:21:33,271
‎Some guy threw it away,
‎and I picked it up.

258
00:21:33,355 --> 00:21:35,273
‎Did you see his face?

259
00:21:57,796 --> 00:21:59,381
‎This looks expensive.

260
00:22:02,175 --> 00:22:03,093
‎Hey, mister.

261
00:22:03,718 --> 00:22:04,636
‎Ta-da.

262
00:22:05,262 --> 00:22:06,346
‎Want to trade?

263
00:22:11,643 --> 00:22:13,145
‎What exactly did I do wrong?

264
00:22:13,228 --> 00:22:16,022
‎The owner threw it away in the trash can.

265
00:22:16,606 --> 00:22:17,441
‎Sir.

266
00:22:18,275 --> 00:22:20,485
‎Do you remember anything about the car?

267
00:22:20,569 --> 00:22:22,279
‎The plate number, model, or color?

268
00:22:22,362 --> 00:22:23,822
‎What about his appearance or build?

269
00:22:23,905 --> 00:22:24,906
‎How many people was he with?

270
00:22:24,990 --> 00:22:27,409
‎How am I supposed to remember all that?

271
00:22:32,330 --> 00:22:34,749
‎Please try to remember. Please.

272
00:22:36,251 --> 00:22:37,294
‎I'm begging you.

273
00:22:40,172 --> 00:22:42,299
‎The car was…

274
00:22:43,091 --> 00:22:45,051
‎It was a white BMV.

275
00:22:45,135 --> 00:22:46,720
‎I didn't see the plate number.

276
00:22:46,803 --> 00:22:47,846
‎What time was it?

277
00:22:48,889 --> 00:22:49,973
‎It was at night.

278
00:22:50,056 --> 00:22:51,224
‎I don't know the exact time.

279
00:22:51,808 --> 00:22:52,726
‎Oh.

280
00:22:52,809 --> 00:22:53,810
‎He had a man bun.

281
00:22:54,561 --> 00:22:55,979
‎That's all I know.

282
00:22:56,062 --> 00:22:57,147
‎Jeez.

283
00:23:00,734 --> 00:23:04,112
‎The weather at Myeongpo Port
‎will be mostly clear during the day,

284
00:23:04,196 --> 00:23:06,781
‎but it will turn cloudy starting tonight.

285
00:23:06,865 --> 00:23:11,369
‎Caution is advised as localized downpours,
‎along with thunder and lightning,

286
00:23:11,453 --> 00:23:12,621
‎are expected tonight.

287
00:23:16,166 --> 00:23:17,167
‎Hello, boss.

288
00:23:17,250 --> 00:23:18,501
‎Hey.

289
00:23:19,377 --> 00:23:21,504
‎Good job securing the warehouse.

290
00:23:21,588 --> 00:23:22,839
‎-Thank you, sir.
‎-Is it this way?

291
00:23:22,923 --> 00:23:24,132
‎Have you eaten yet?

292
00:23:24,216 --> 00:23:25,342
‎Yes, I did.

293
00:23:26,301 --> 00:23:28,220
‎Hey, Gang-min. Have we eaten yet?

294
00:23:28,303 --> 00:23:30,931
‎No, we haven't had a single meal today.

295
00:23:31,014 --> 00:23:34,809
‎Man, the kid here says he already ate.

296
00:23:34,893 --> 00:23:37,479
‎It's like he doesn't give a damn
‎if I starve to death or not.

297
00:23:38,188 --> 00:23:39,189
‎I'm sorry, sir.

298
00:23:40,982 --> 00:23:41,942
‎I'm just kidding.

299
00:23:42,901 --> 00:23:43,777
‎What did you have?

300
00:23:44,402 --> 00:23:46,404
‎I had blood sausage soup, sir.

301
00:23:46,488 --> 00:23:47,447
‎Was it good?

302
00:23:48,114 --> 00:23:50,075
‎It wasn't bad, sir.

303
00:23:50,158 --> 00:23:51,952
‎Then you should wash it down
‎with some water!

304
00:23:54,913 --> 00:23:57,374
‎Hurry the hell up if you're done drinking!

305
00:23:57,457 --> 00:23:59,000
‎-Everyone else will be here soon!
‎-Sir!

306
00:23:59,084 --> 00:24:00,210
‎Should we move the body, boss?

307
00:24:01,169 --> 00:24:03,088
‎Let's eat first, you punk.

308
00:24:04,422 --> 00:24:05,799
‎Sounds good, sir.

309
00:24:16,184 --> 00:24:19,062
‎We don't know the exact time,
‎so look for the homeless man.

310
00:24:19,145 --> 00:24:19,980
‎Okay.

311
00:24:20,563 --> 00:24:22,732
‎A white BMV…

312
00:24:35,829 --> 00:24:36,705
‎There. Found him.

313
00:24:36,788 --> 00:24:38,581
‎You did? Who is it? Do you see his face?

314
00:24:38,665 --> 00:24:39,499
‎Just a second.

315
00:24:48,675 --> 00:24:49,759
‎It's loading.

316
00:24:50,927 --> 00:24:52,679
‎Kim Sang-man, 41 years old.

317
00:24:52,762 --> 00:24:54,848
‎-Eight priors?
‎-What?

318
00:24:54,931 --> 00:24:56,016
‎Eight priors?

319
00:24:56,599 --> 00:24:59,019
‎Eight priors for violent crimes?
‎Are you serious?

320
00:24:59,102 --> 00:24:59,936
‎Hold on.

321
00:25:01,563 --> 00:25:02,897
‎He got out of the back seat.

322
00:25:02,981 --> 00:25:04,858
‎-That means there were others.
‎-Okay.

323
00:25:06,484 --> 00:25:08,278
‎If we plug in the vehicle search data

324
00:25:09,404 --> 00:25:10,822
‎to track its location…

325
00:25:12,365 --> 00:25:13,325
‎Just a second.

326
00:25:16,828 --> 00:25:19,372
‎It's searching in real-time,
‎so it'll take a moment to load.

327
00:25:20,415 --> 00:25:22,125
‎How dare they do that to Min-ji?

328
00:25:22,208 --> 00:25:24,586
‎Kim Sang-man.

329
00:25:26,671 --> 00:25:27,714
‎Speed bump.

330
00:25:30,175 --> 00:25:31,176
‎You idiot!

331
00:25:31,926 --> 00:25:33,053
‎You're killing me.

332
00:25:34,804 --> 00:25:38,183
‎We brought the body
‎and secured a location.

333
00:25:38,266 --> 00:25:41,936
‎Now all that's left
‎is to drop this bombshell on Ju Gang-chan.

334
00:25:46,399 --> 00:25:47,525
‎"Hey, Gang-chan."

335
00:25:48,777 --> 00:25:49,903
‎"Your daughter…

336
00:25:51,279 --> 00:25:53,114
‎killed a person."

337
00:26:04,876 --> 00:26:06,169
‎But sir,

338
00:26:06,252 --> 00:26:08,630
‎why are you so obsessed with Ju Gang-chan?

339
00:26:09,631 --> 00:26:12,884
‎Did he screw you over big time
‎a while back or something?

340
00:26:13,760 --> 00:26:15,845
‎Boss, here's a big potato for you.

341
00:26:30,693 --> 00:26:31,569
‎You little!

342
00:26:33,738 --> 00:26:35,031
‎I'm sorry, sir!

343
00:26:40,620 --> 00:26:42,122
‎Please forgive me!

344
00:26:50,547 --> 00:26:52,132
‎9 YEARS AGO

345
00:26:52,215 --> 00:26:54,008
‎-No to redevelopment!
‎-No to redevelopment!

346
00:26:54,092 --> 00:26:56,719
‎-Go away!
‎-Go away!

347
00:26:56,803 --> 00:26:57,762
‎-Bring it on.
‎-Go away!

348
00:26:57,846 --> 00:26:59,013
‎All of you!

349
00:26:59,597 --> 00:27:00,849
‎STOP RECONSTRUCTION
‎THAT DESTROYS CITIZENS' LIVES

350
00:27:00,932 --> 00:27:03,268
‎Do you know how old these apartments are?

351
00:27:03,351 --> 00:27:04,519
‎I'm not sure, sir.

352
00:27:04,602 --> 00:27:06,146
‎Forty years.

353
00:27:06,229 --> 00:27:08,690
‎These 40-year-old apartments
‎still aren't approved for reconstruction.

354
00:27:08,773 --> 00:27:11,734
‎You and I both need that approval
‎to make a fortune.

355
00:27:11,818 --> 00:27:12,652
‎Don't you agree?

356
00:27:14,237 --> 00:27:15,113
‎Boss.

357
00:27:15,196 --> 00:27:18,950
‎How many apartments these days
‎still don't have underground parking?

358
00:27:37,093 --> 00:27:41,055
‎We're at the scene at Midu Apartments
‎where a cleaning service employee fell.

359
00:27:41,139 --> 00:27:42,474
‎Employee A

360
00:27:42,557 --> 00:27:47,020
‎fell off the railing and was transported
‎to the hospital for surgery,

361
00:27:47,103 --> 00:27:49,564
‎but hasn't regained consciousness.

362
00:27:49,647 --> 00:27:51,733
‎Concerns are mounting over building safety

363
00:27:51,816 --> 00:27:54,819
‎as residents describe the hallways
‎as unsafe due to low railings.

364
00:27:54,903 --> 00:27:57,363
‎With cracks appearing
‎across the exterior walls,

365
00:27:57,447 --> 00:28:02,285
‎many say that simple repairs
‎can no longer hold the building together.

366
00:28:03,953 --> 00:28:09,375
‎Midu Apartments' reconstruction
‎has been approved after years of setbacks.

367
00:28:09,459 --> 00:28:10,835
‎The Seoul Metropolitan Government

368
00:28:10,919 --> 00:28:12,795
‎announced on the 19th
‎that they have passed the decision

369
00:28:12,879 --> 00:28:15,924
‎to authorize the reconstruction plan
‎for the 40-year-old Midu Apartments.

370
00:28:16,007 --> 00:28:19,302
‎According to experts, this authorization…

371
00:28:24,516 --> 00:28:27,018
‎I didn't have a choice.
‎I was ordered to do it.

372
00:28:27,101 --> 00:28:29,145
‎Jung-dae,
‎please forgive me just this once.

373
00:28:29,229 --> 00:28:30,480
‎Jung-dae, please!

374
00:28:36,319 --> 00:28:38,821
‎I didn't want to take over like this.

375
00:28:38,905 --> 00:28:39,739
‎CEO YANG SEOK-CHEOL

376
00:28:43,243 --> 00:28:46,037
‎Who knew it was so damn easy
‎to become the boss?

377
00:28:47,080 --> 00:28:48,498
‎I should've done this sooner.

378
00:28:55,129 --> 00:28:56,673
‎Just trust me

379
00:28:57,340 --> 00:28:58,299
‎and don't waver.

380
00:28:58,383 --> 00:28:59,926
‎Here's a toast

381
00:29:00,885 --> 00:29:02,095
‎to our future.

382
00:29:02,178 --> 00:29:04,222
‎-Cheers!
‎-Cheers!

383
00:29:06,808 --> 00:29:07,976
‎-Bring in the band.
‎-Yes, sir.

384
00:29:09,894 --> 00:29:10,979
‎Boss, you got a call.

385
00:29:12,397 --> 00:29:13,523
‎Everyone, be quiet.

386
00:29:14,357 --> 00:29:15,191
‎Who's this?

387
00:29:15,775 --> 00:29:17,694
‎This is the executive office
‎of Juhak Construction.

388
00:29:17,777 --> 00:29:19,487
‎The chairman would like to see you.

389
00:29:31,749 --> 00:29:33,918
‎I heard there was a new head
‎of the company.

390
00:29:34,544 --> 00:29:36,170
‎I didn't know
‎it was the guy under Mr. Yang.

391
00:29:38,131 --> 00:29:40,133
‎I guess you're pretty capable
‎for a young guy.

392
00:29:41,259 --> 00:29:42,635
‎I look forward to working with you.

393
00:29:42,719 --> 00:29:44,262
‎There's a lot I need you to do for me.

394
00:29:46,681 --> 00:29:48,850
‎I forgot all about you for a minute there.

395
00:29:49,976 --> 00:29:51,019
‎It was you, right?

396
00:29:52,645 --> 00:29:55,481
‎The bastard
‎who ordered Mr. Yang to kill me.

397
00:29:56,608 --> 00:29:57,734
‎It's okay.

398
00:30:00,278 --> 00:30:01,946
‎I think there's a misunderstanding.

399
00:30:02,447 --> 00:30:03,781
‎I never ordered him to do that.

400
00:30:05,033 --> 00:30:08,620
‎I just muttered to myself
‎that I wished someone would die there.

401
00:30:09,245 --> 00:30:10,163
‎What?

402
00:30:11,247 --> 00:30:12,123
‎I have to say…

403
00:30:13,875 --> 00:30:16,502
‎Mr. Yang was quite an incompetent man.

404
00:30:18,588 --> 00:30:19,964
‎Look at you. You're still alive.

405
00:30:24,802 --> 00:30:25,637
‎Crush him.

406
00:30:30,266 --> 00:30:31,100
‎Bring it!

407
00:30:38,232 --> 00:30:39,275
‎Die, you asshole!

408
00:31:55,810 --> 00:31:59,230
‎When I was young,
‎my next-door neighbor had a huge dog.

409
00:32:04,861 --> 00:32:08,156
‎But you see, the dog was vicious
‎and bit their owner a few times.

410
00:32:08,740 --> 00:32:12,452
‎The owner couldn't take it anymore
‎and was about to put it down.

411
00:32:14,412 --> 00:32:17,040
‎But I convinced them that I could tame it.

412
00:32:19,333 --> 00:32:21,794
‎You see, I liked the dog
‎because it was vicious.

413
00:32:31,345 --> 00:32:33,765
‎Do you know how I tamed it?

414
00:32:38,728 --> 00:32:41,689
‎I made sure it could never bite its owner.

415
00:33:23,189 --> 00:33:24,398
‎Open your mouth.

416
00:33:39,372 --> 00:33:42,083
‎Do you feel like wagging your tail now?

417
00:33:42,667 --> 00:33:44,502
‎I could also pour boiling water
‎down your throat

418
00:33:44,585 --> 00:33:46,629
‎and make sure you can't even bark.

419
00:33:56,639 --> 00:33:58,307
‎I'll do anything.

420
00:33:58,975 --> 00:34:01,018
‎I'll do whatever you want.

421
00:34:01,102 --> 00:34:04,355
‎I'll become your dog, sir.

422
00:34:06,065 --> 00:34:07,358
‎Please don't kill me.

423
00:34:09,694 --> 00:34:10,611
‎Please spare me.

424
00:34:19,704 --> 00:34:21,247
‎The sun's down.

425
00:34:21,330 --> 00:34:23,541
‎Let's wrap up here and move the body.

426
00:34:23,624 --> 00:34:24,458
‎-Yes, sir.
‎-Yes, sir.

427
00:34:44,812 --> 00:34:48,482
‎Jeez, what kind of thug walks on eggshells
‎after taking a few hits?

428
00:34:49,984 --> 00:34:51,569
‎Did it hurt a lot?

429
00:34:51,652 --> 00:34:53,029
‎No, sir. I'm okay, sir!

430
00:34:56,949 --> 00:34:58,075
‎We're here, boss.

431
00:34:58,159 --> 00:34:59,452
‎I know that, idiot!

432
00:35:00,036 --> 00:35:00,912
‎Yes, sir!

433
00:35:28,856 --> 00:35:31,484
‎This dead body weighs a ton, boss.

434
00:35:31,567 --> 00:35:32,610
‎Stop whining.

435
00:35:38,908 --> 00:35:39,742
‎Excuse me.

436
00:35:40,743 --> 00:35:41,577
‎What are you doing?

437
00:35:46,707 --> 00:35:47,541
‎What's that?

438
00:35:50,127 --> 00:35:51,921
‎-It's a dead body.
‎-What?

439
00:35:52,588 --> 00:35:53,506
‎A dead body?

440
00:35:54,882 --> 00:35:58,094
‎You should've gone to bed early, old man.

441
00:35:58,177 --> 00:35:59,512
‎Hey, Sang-man.

442
00:35:59,595 --> 00:36:00,429
‎Yes, boss.

443
00:36:04,016 --> 00:36:05,768
‎It's not what you think, sir.

444
00:36:05,851 --> 00:36:07,812
‎We rented this cold storage warehouse.

445
00:36:08,396 --> 00:36:09,772
‎Let me show you the contract.

446
00:36:10,523 --> 00:36:11,691
‎Where was it again?

447
00:36:13,567 --> 00:36:14,402
‎Hey!

448
00:36:19,615 --> 00:36:21,701
‎Still nothing?
‎How much longer will it take?

449
00:36:23,452 --> 00:36:25,288
‎Almost there. 80%.

450
00:36:26,789 --> 00:36:28,207
‎Now at 81%.

451
00:36:28,291 --> 00:36:30,251
‎Jeez, it's taking forever.

452
00:36:40,761 --> 00:36:42,847
‎Oh boy, this is heavy.

453
00:36:53,441 --> 00:36:54,775
‎Now at 95%.

454
00:36:58,029 --> 00:36:59,322
‎Okay, 96%.

455
00:37:10,249 --> 00:37:11,083
‎What's that?

456
00:37:13,294 --> 00:37:14,628
‎Isn't that Mole Cricket?

457
00:37:15,838 --> 00:37:16,839
‎What?

458
00:38:53,894 --> 00:38:57,731
‎MYEONGPO PORT, REPUBLIC OF KOREA

459
00:39:09,452 --> 00:39:10,870
‎Hey, Kim.

460
00:39:10,953 --> 00:39:12,496
‎I know you're not dead, so come out.

461
00:39:13,456 --> 00:39:15,374
‎Stalling will only make things
‎worse for you.

462
00:39:15,458 --> 00:39:19,712
‎You know you're better off coming with me
‎than being dragged to the North to die.

463
00:39:20,880 --> 00:39:21,755
‎Come on out!

464
00:39:35,311 --> 00:39:37,438
‎Not you. I want Kim.

465
00:39:37,980 --> 00:39:38,939
‎Hurry up!

466
00:39:41,150 --> 00:39:41,984
‎You know,

467
00:39:42,610 --> 00:39:46,447
‎I didn't like you the moment you showed up
‎wearing that fedora.

468
00:39:48,491 --> 00:39:54,038
‎You have no idea
‎how big of a mistake you just made.

469
00:39:54,788 --> 00:39:58,042
‎I'm extremely angry right now,

470
00:39:58,125 --> 00:40:00,085
‎and I'm going to express that anger.

471
00:40:01,170 --> 00:40:02,087
‎Give me a second.

472
00:40:08,761 --> 00:40:10,137
‎-What are you doing?
‎-You know,

473
00:40:11,013 --> 00:40:12,473
‎my knees

474
00:40:13,516 --> 00:40:15,643
‎and my back hurt, so I can't do it much.

475
00:40:17,019 --> 00:40:18,521
‎But I feel like I should do it today,

476
00:40:19,605 --> 00:40:21,023
‎and I think I can.

477
00:40:22,024 --> 00:40:24,652
‎Stop playing games and get out of the way.

478
00:40:24,735 --> 00:40:26,403
‎Don't you know who I am, you bastard?

479
00:40:26,946 --> 00:40:27,780
‎You?

480
00:40:29,114 --> 00:40:30,199
‎Mole…

481
00:40:31,575 --> 00:40:33,369
‎Mole Rat, right?

482
00:40:33,452 --> 00:40:35,829
‎You're a mole rat.

483
00:40:35,913 --> 00:40:37,373
‎You're a mole rat.

484
00:40:37,456 --> 00:40:40,584
‎I bet you got that fedora off the streets.

485
00:41:16,704 --> 00:41:17,871
‎It worked.

486
00:41:19,832 --> 00:41:21,083
‎I did it.

487
00:41:24,128 --> 00:41:24,962
‎You see that?

488
00:41:25,045 --> 00:41:27,840
‎You think a fancy move like that
‎would work in a real fight?

489
00:41:29,592 --> 00:41:30,426
‎Maybe not.

490
00:41:31,302 --> 00:41:32,303
‎But still,

491
00:41:32,845 --> 00:41:34,513
‎I managed to distract you.

492
00:41:35,514 --> 00:41:36,682
‎Right, Mole Rat?

493
00:41:39,977 --> 00:41:41,270
‎Kim!

494
00:41:51,030 --> 00:41:52,906
‎Oh, come on.

495
00:41:52,990 --> 00:41:54,908
‎Did you just pull out a knife?

496
00:41:54,992 --> 00:41:56,201
‎Can't handle me barehanded?

497
00:41:57,578 --> 00:41:58,495
‎Bring it.

498
00:42:07,046 --> 00:42:07,880
‎I can't be bothered.

499
00:42:08,505 --> 00:42:09,381
‎Right.

500
00:42:10,174 --> 00:42:12,384
‎The hero always shows up at the end.

501
00:42:16,847 --> 00:42:18,307
‎You've got this, Taekwondo!

502
00:42:27,858 --> 00:42:30,444
‎I guess you're not a total waste
‎of taxpayers' money.

503
00:42:31,070 --> 00:42:32,946
‎Let's see how you fight on that leg.

504
00:42:35,741 --> 00:42:36,867
‎Look, over there.

505
00:42:37,493 --> 00:42:41,288
‎The director and Sung Han-soo
‎are facing off up ahead!

506
00:42:41,872 --> 00:42:44,792
‎You brought guns, knives,
‎and‎ your friends, huh?

507
00:42:44,875 --> 00:42:46,794
‎Shut up and bring it.

508
00:42:51,215 --> 00:42:52,591
‎Have you ever gone bungee jumping?

509
00:43:01,767 --> 00:43:02,601
‎Jeez, my back.

510
00:43:05,062 --> 00:43:06,605
‎See you, Park Jin-cheol.

511
00:43:18,617 --> 00:43:19,993
‎-Director!
‎-Director!

512
00:43:20,077 --> 00:43:21,787
‎-Director!
‎-What should we do?

513
00:43:21,870 --> 00:43:23,288
‎He can't swim, can he?

514
00:43:30,045 --> 00:43:31,714
‎Is it my turn now?

515
00:43:36,969 --> 00:43:38,512
‎Two, four,

516
00:43:39,096 --> 00:43:41,014
‎six, eight, ten…

517
00:43:42,391 --> 00:43:43,726
‎Fourteen total.

518
00:43:43,809 --> 00:43:44,685
‎Let's do this.

519
00:43:46,895 --> 00:43:47,980
‎I surrender.

520
00:43:51,275 --> 00:43:52,109
‎Peace!

521
00:43:53,652 --> 00:43:54,820
‎I want peace!

522
00:44:16,592 --> 00:44:17,509
‎Min-ji.

523
00:44:19,052 --> 00:44:20,304
‎Just be alive.

524
00:44:21,638 --> 00:44:22,473
‎Please.

525
00:44:50,501 --> 00:44:51,418
‎Hello?

526
00:44:53,337 --> 00:44:54,171
‎I'm…

527
00:44:55,964 --> 00:44:57,424
‎I'm in here!

528
00:45:02,804 --> 00:45:04,264
‎I'm in here!

529
00:45:05,265 --> 00:45:07,726
‎Help! I'm in here!

530
00:45:25,536 --> 00:45:26,954
‎JU GANG-CHAN'S LACKEY

531
00:45:27,037 --> 00:45:28,997
‎You guys are in big trouble now.

532
00:45:31,083 --> 00:45:33,752
‎Why the hell isn't Nam answering?

533
00:45:34,378 --> 00:45:36,088
‎-Hey, Sang-man.
‎-Yes, boss?

534
00:45:36,171 --> 00:45:39,091
‎Go to the warehouse and take a photo.

535
00:45:39,174 --> 00:45:42,010
‎Not just of the body.
‎Take a selfie with it.

536
00:45:42,761 --> 00:45:43,595
‎Hey.

537
00:45:44,221 --> 00:45:45,681
‎You know what I mean, right?

538
00:45:45,764 --> 00:45:46,848
‎Yes.

539
00:45:46,932 --> 00:45:48,225
‎So you're saying

540
00:45:48,308 --> 00:45:52,271
‎I should take a photo of the body first,
‎and then one of myself, right?

541
00:45:53,939 --> 00:45:54,773
‎You idiot.

542
00:45:56,650 --> 00:45:58,527
‎Take a selfie with the body like this.

543
00:45:59,903 --> 00:46:00,904
‎Jeez.

544
00:46:02,239 --> 00:46:04,449
‎You know what? Just forget it.

545
00:46:08,579 --> 00:46:11,415
‎Get a haircut
‎so your brain can get some oxygen.

546
00:46:12,040 --> 00:46:13,333
‎Or lose some weight.

547
00:46:13,834 --> 00:46:14,710
‎Hey.

548
00:46:15,669 --> 00:46:18,422
‎You're supposed to take a selfie
‎before you take a photo of the body.

549
00:46:18,505 --> 00:46:19,339
‎Shut it.

550
00:46:42,112 --> 00:46:43,780
‎I can't trust them to do anything.

551
00:46:51,830 --> 00:46:53,790
‎Hey, Nam.

552
00:46:53,874 --> 00:46:56,001
‎Why didn't you pick up?

553
00:46:56,084 --> 00:46:57,502
‎Don't you miss me?

554
00:46:58,545 --> 00:47:03,634
‎I was actually wondering
‎if I should send you a photo or not.

555
00:47:04,551 --> 00:47:05,927
‎Just get to the point.

556
00:47:06,011 --> 00:47:08,597
‎I called because I missed you, of course.

557
00:47:08,680 --> 00:47:12,309
‎You still walking around
‎with that weasel-ass face?

558
00:47:13,560 --> 00:47:14,394
‎Do you want to die?

559
00:47:17,022 --> 00:47:19,483
‎Okay, okay. Jeez, you're scary.

560
00:47:20,984 --> 00:47:24,363
‎I need to talk to Chairman Ju.

561
00:47:24,446 --> 00:47:26,448
‎Put Chairman Ju… No, wait.

562
00:47:27,074 --> 00:47:29,159
‎Put Gang-chan on the phone.

563
00:47:29,743 --> 00:47:31,078
‎So you really do want to die.

564
00:47:31,161 --> 00:47:32,037
‎Where are you?

565
00:47:32,120 --> 00:47:35,082
‎That bastard's daughter
‎is the one who wants to die, not me.

566
00:47:35,707 --> 00:47:38,001
‎She killed someone, you see.

567
00:47:39,294 --> 00:47:42,673
‎If he doesn't want his precious daughter
‎to go to prison,

568
00:47:42,756 --> 00:47:45,425
‎tell him to call me right now.

569
00:47:46,009 --> 00:47:49,179
‎I'll take good care of the body
‎in the meantime.

570
00:47:51,848 --> 00:47:52,683
‎What

571
00:48:02,651 --> 00:48:04,277
‎WORTHLESS THUG
‎VOICE RECORDING

572
00:48:04,361 --> 00:48:07,364
‎Are you saying you killed this student?

573
00:48:07,447 --> 00:48:09,866
‎Tell me.
‎You can take care of the body, right?

574
00:48:11,368 --> 00:48:13,995
‎You're scaring me.
‎Why are you asking me this?

575
00:48:14,079 --> 00:48:15,831
‎Money isn't a problem.

576
00:48:15,914 --> 00:48:17,499
‎I'll give you as much as you want.

577
00:48:17,582 --> 00:48:20,043
‎No, forget it!
‎I'll pretend I didn't hear that.

578
00:48:20,127 --> 00:48:21,336
‎Go away!

579
00:48:25,465 --> 00:48:27,217
‎I was studying in the study room

580
00:48:27,843 --> 00:48:29,344
‎and stepped out for a break

581
00:48:29,970 --> 00:48:32,139
‎when she showed up
‎and started cursing me out.

582
00:48:33,515 --> 00:48:34,850
‎So you killed her?

583
00:48:34,933 --> 00:48:36,560
‎No, I didn't! She just…

584
00:48:38,270 --> 00:48:41,398
‎All I did was nudge her out of the way,
‎but she just fell on her own.

585
00:48:43,150 --> 00:48:44,401
‎I think she did it on purpose.

586
00:48:45,068 --> 00:48:47,154
‎She was pulling an act
‎to scam me for medical bills.

587
00:48:50,449 --> 00:48:51,867
‎Dad!

588
00:48:52,951 --> 00:48:54,578
‎You know she's crazy.

589
00:48:55,579 --> 00:48:57,038
‎She bullied me every day.

590
00:48:59,082 --> 00:49:00,208
‎I didn't do anything wrong.

591
00:49:01,376 --> 00:49:02,878
‎It wasn't my fault, Dad.

592
00:49:10,677 --> 00:49:12,554
‎You have to be honest with me.

593
00:49:13,138 --> 00:49:14,181
‎Be honest.

594
00:49:14,264 --> 00:49:15,098
‎Did you…

595
00:49:16,767 --> 00:49:18,018
‎kill her?

596
00:49:20,270 --> 00:49:21,688
‎I think so.

597
00:49:33,825 --> 00:49:37,120
‎If you wanted to kill her,
‎you should've asked me to do it.

598
00:49:38,205 --> 00:49:39,539
‎I'd do anything for you.

599
00:49:43,668 --> 00:49:45,796
‎I've always given you
‎whatever you asked for.

600
00:49:47,047 --> 00:49:48,715
‎It really hurts
‎that you didn't come to me.

601
00:49:49,883 --> 00:49:51,426
‎I'm sorry, Dad.

602
00:49:55,263 --> 00:49:56,097
‎It's not a big deal.

603
00:49:57,808 --> 00:49:58,683
‎It's okay.

604
00:50:01,186 --> 00:50:02,312
‎It's okay.

605
00:50:08,443 --> 00:50:09,653
‎Did you check if she was dead?

606
00:50:13,406 --> 00:50:14,991
‎She was bleeding from her head,

607
00:50:16,660 --> 00:50:17,828
‎but I'm not sure.

608
00:50:31,341 --> 00:50:33,468
‎Golden Teeth has the body, right?

609
00:50:33,552 --> 00:50:34,386
‎Yes.

610
00:50:36,471 --> 00:50:38,431
‎Then make it so that ‎he‎ killed her.

611
00:50:38,515 --> 00:50:39,516
‎Understood, sir.

612
00:51:13,842 --> 00:51:15,135
‎Hello?

613
00:51:15,218 --> 00:51:16,761
‎Please open the door!

614
00:51:17,470 --> 00:51:18,930
‎Hello?

615
00:51:19,014 --> 00:51:20,599
‎Is anyone there?

616
00:51:22,851 --> 00:51:24,227
‎Please open the door!

617
00:51:32,110 --> 00:51:33,403
‎Please open the door…

618
00:53:32,939 --> 00:53:34,149
‎I'm cold…

619
00:53:35,316 --> 00:53:36,359
‎Dad…

620
00:53:58,673 --> 00:53:59,883
‎I'm cold…

621
00:54:46,346 --> 00:54:47,347
‎Who are you?

622
00:54:47,430 --> 00:54:49,265
‎Jeez, you scared me.

623
00:54:49,349 --> 00:54:51,184
‎Who are you, mister? Why are you here?

624
00:54:54,521 --> 00:54:56,981
‎-Who the hell are you?
‎-I asked you a question!

625
00:55:01,236 --> 00:55:03,780
‎NAME: KIM SANG-MAN
‎AGE: 41

626
00:55:03,863 --> 00:55:07,117
‎Does this bastard
‎have wax in his ears or something?

627
00:55:07,200 --> 00:55:09,327
‎I just asked who the hell you are!

628
00:55:10,912 --> 00:55:12,705
‎What the hell's wrong with him?

629
00:55:17,085 --> 00:55:18,753
‎You know whose phone this is, don't you?

630
00:55:20,797 --> 00:55:22,257
‎Where is she?

631
00:55:27,303 --> 00:55:29,931
‎You're putting me in a tough spot.

632
00:55:30,014 --> 00:55:32,225
‎You asked for this, okay?

633
00:55:42,819 --> 00:55:43,778
‎To the left.

634
00:55:48,283 --> 00:55:49,367
‎Oh man.

635
00:55:50,827 --> 00:55:52,495
‎Even a dead body
‎would freeze to death here.

636
00:56:02,922 --> 00:56:05,300
‎Where did they put it?

637
00:56:18,813 --> 00:56:20,398
‎JU GANG-CHAN

638
00:57:03,024 --> 00:57:04,901
‎Goodness, Chairman.

639
00:57:04,984 --> 00:57:07,195
‎How kind of you to call me.

640
00:57:08,279 --> 00:57:09,113
‎I hope you're well.

641
00:57:09,989 --> 00:57:14,244
‎Well, I suppose
‎you're in much better shape than me

642
00:57:14,327 --> 00:57:16,454
‎since you only eat what's good for you.

643
00:57:20,833 --> 00:57:22,418
‎Chief Nam filled me in.

644
00:57:23,628 --> 00:57:25,421
‎I heard you did my daughter a favor.

645
00:57:25,505 --> 00:57:28,633
‎Goodness, there are no favors between us.

646
00:57:28,716 --> 00:57:32,637
‎How's your blonde-haired daughter doing?

647
00:57:32,720 --> 00:57:36,266
‎They say early education
‎is important these days.

648
00:57:36,349 --> 00:57:39,894
‎She takes after her father
‎and knows how to kill people

649
00:57:39,978 --> 00:57:42,564
‎and get rid of bodies very well.

650
00:57:42,647 --> 00:57:45,733
‎You raised a very smart daughter.

651
00:57:46,568 --> 00:57:47,652
‎Let's talk in person.

652
00:57:47,735 --> 00:57:49,070
‎Of course.

653
00:57:50,738 --> 00:57:51,573
‎But…

654
00:57:52,365 --> 00:57:55,577
‎stop talking down to me, asshole.

655
00:57:55,660 --> 00:57:56,911
‎Don't you get it?

656
00:57:58,413 --> 00:58:00,665
‎I'll send you an address.

657
00:58:01,874 --> 00:58:04,794
‎Get your ass over here right now
‎with two billion won in cash.

658
00:58:05,920 --> 00:58:07,922
‎And leave your lackeys behind.

659
00:58:08,006 --> 00:58:09,632
‎Come alone.

660
00:58:10,341 --> 00:58:11,426
‎Oh, and one more thing.

661
00:58:11,509 --> 00:58:14,012
‎It's about Nam's teeth.

662
00:58:14,762 --> 00:58:16,723
‎Pull them all out and bring them to me.

663
00:58:16,806 --> 00:58:18,933
‎I'll need a photo as proof as well.

664
00:58:19,017 --> 00:58:21,853
‎He won't be able to talk properly
‎without his teeth,

665
00:58:21,936 --> 00:58:24,230
‎but tell him I'll give him
‎private lessons for that.

666
00:58:28,818 --> 00:58:30,778
‎-Let's go.
‎-Yes, sir.

667
00:58:35,033 --> 00:58:35,867
‎Let's go!

668
00:58:35,950 --> 00:58:37,076
‎-Yes, sir!
‎-Yes, sir!

669
00:58:57,221 --> 00:58:58,848
‎SHARING LOCATION WITH KIM MIN-JI

670
00:59:13,488 --> 00:59:16,658
‎23, Hangman 10-ro.

671
00:59:17,950 --> 00:59:21,871
‎Damn, I really want to see that bastard
‎get his teeth yanked out.

672
00:59:21,954 --> 00:59:23,623
‎Maybe I should've told him
‎to bring him here.

673
01:00:46,664 --> 01:00:50,084
‎AGENT KIM REACTIVATED

674
01:00:50,626 --> 01:00:51,502
‎I'm sorry.

675
01:00:52,712 --> 01:00:53,629
‎I'll wait for you.

676
01:00:53,713 --> 01:00:55,715
‎I don't have time for this. Bring it.

677
01:00:56,299 --> 01:00:58,426
‎Don't you think we'll need weapons too?

678
01:00:59,302 --> 01:01:01,929
‎So, his daughter is his weakness.

679
01:01:02,013 --> 01:01:03,097
‎Spread out and search.

680
01:01:03,181 --> 01:01:06,809
‎All we need is for Kim Min-ji
‎to disappear.

681
01:01:08,352 --> 01:01:10,772
‎If you so much as lay a finger
‎on my daughter,

682
01:01:11,939 --> 01:01:13,441
‎I'll kill you all.

683
01:01:14,233 --> 01:01:15,359
‎I'm sorry, Dad.

684
01:01:15,443 --> 01:01:16,277
‎Min-ji…

685
01:01:18,237 --> 01:01:19,363
‎is alive.

686
01:01:21,115 --> 01:01:24,076
‎Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim

